<title>PORTUGAL: Analysts see no Portugal rate cut tomorrow.</title>
<headline>Analysts see no Portugal rate cut tomorrow.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six analysts polled by Reuters said they believed that the Bank of Portugal would decide not to ease official rates tomorrow on the eve of a new commercial bank reserve period.</p>
<p>All six analysts agreed that the central bank had room to cut rates further.</p>
<p>1. Will the Bank of Portugal cut its repo rate this week.</p>
<p>No - six analysts.</p>
<p>Yes - 0 analysts.</p>
<p>2. If the answer to question 1 is yes, the rate cut will be by how much?</p>
<p>No - n.a.</p>
<p>Yes -n.a.</p>
<p>3. Could the central bank cut other official rates this week?</p>
<p>No - 6.</p>
<p>Yes - 0.</p>
<p>4. Does the central bank have room to cut rates further?</p>
<p>Yes - 6.</p>
<p>No - 0.</p>
<p>-- Fernanda Pargana, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
